keywords: [steering vectors, activation steering, sparsity, one-bit, interpretability, GPT-1]
abstract: "A sparse activation-steering vector retains exactly the fraction of the full steering effect that its cosine with the dense vector predicts (r = 0.90). Keeping 96 of 768 residual dimensions retains 54-72% of the effect; one-bit sign-only vectors match top-k at every k. Open-weight per-block vectors for GPT-1, code, and all generations are released."
